{{Short description|Japanese virologist}}
{{nihongo|'''Naoki Mori'''|森 直樹|Mori Naoki|extra=}} is a Japanese [[virologist]] who is a professor at the [[University of the Ryukyus]] in [[Okinawa Prefecture]], [[Japan]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=琉球大学研究者データベース - 琉球大学 |url=https://kenkyushadb.lab.u-ryukyu.ac.jp/search?m=home&l=ja |access-date=2022-09-05 |website=kenkyushadb.lab.u-ryukyu.ac.jp}}</ref> He has received numerous awards for his research on [[human T-cell leukemia virus type 1]] (HTLV-1), a [[retrovirus]] which causes [[adult T-cell leukemia]].<ref>[http://www.ajcancer.ipp-shr.cqu.edu.au/issues/profile.php?issueid=34 Profile: Professor Naoki Mori], ''Austral-Asian Journal of Cancer'', January 2008</ref><ref name="science">{{cite web | first = Dennis | last = Normile | work = [[Science (journal)|Science]] | url = http://news.sciencemag.org/scienceinsider/2011/01/japanese-virologist-loses-job.html | title = Japanese Virologist Loses Job, Gets Publishing Ban for Image Manipulation | date = 19 January 2011 | access-date = October 27, 2011 | url-status = dead | archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20120130043645/http://news.sciencemag.org/scienceinsider/2011/01/japanese-virologist-loses-job.html | archive-date = 30 January 2012 }}</ref>

==Research fraud==
In 2010, [[Retraction Watch]] reported that five of Mori's papers had been [[retractions in academic publishing|retracted]] by the journal ''[[Infection and Immunity]]''.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Marcus |first=Adam |date=25 December 2010 |title=Japanese virologist hit with publishing ban after widespread data manipulation |url=https://retractionwatch.com/2010/12/24/japanese-virologist-hit-with-publishing-ban-after-widespread-data-manipulation/ |access-date=5 September 2022 |website=[[Retraction Watch]]}}</ref> (The ''New York Times'' later put that figure at six.)<ref>{{Cite web |last=Zimmer |first=Carl |date=16 April 2012 |title=Rise in Scientific Journal Retractions Prompts Calls for Reform |url=http://www.nytimes.com/2012/04/17/science/rise-in-scientific-journal-retractions-prompts-calls-for-reform.html?_r=1 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120417232759/http://www.nytimes.com/2012/04/17/science/rise-in-scientific-journal-retractions-prompts-calls-for-reform.html?_r=1 |archive-date=17 April 2012 |access-date=5 September 2022 |website=[[The New York Times]]}}</ref> The papers, which were published between 2000 and 2009, described studies on ''[[Helicobacter pylori|H. pylori]]''.<ref name="science"/><ref name="retraction-watch1">{{cite web |last=Marcus |first=Adam |date=24 December 2010 |title=Japanese virologist hit with publishing ban after widespread data manipulation |url=http://retractionwatch.wordpress.com/2010/12/24/japanese-virologist-hit-with-publishing-ban-after-widespread-data-manipulation/ |access-date=October 27, 2011 |website=Retraction Watch |publisher=}}</ref> Mori was banned for ten years from publishing articles in journals operated by the [[American Society for Microbiology]] after it was determined that he had manipulated data and images in a number of articles.<ref name="science"/> By October 2011, 30 papers coauthored by Mori had been retracted, including five from ''Infection and Immunity'', seven from the ''[[International Journal of Cancer]]'',<ref name="retraction-watch2">{{cite web |last=Marcus |first=Adam |date=12 October 2011 |title=That's a Mori! Seven more retractions brings latest count to 30 |url=http://retractionwatch.wordpress.com/2011/10/12/thats-a-mori-seven-more-retractions-brings-latest-count-to-30/#more-4770 |website=Retraction Watch |publisher=}}</ref> two from ''[[Blood (journal)|Blood]]'', and one from [[Biochemical and Biophysical Research Communications]] titled "Downregulation of citrin, a mitochondrial AGC, is associated with apoptosis of hepatocytes''"''.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Marcus |first=Adam |date=10 October 2011 |title=Another retraction for Naoki Mori (make that 23?) |url=http://retractionwatch.com/2011/10/10/another-retraction-for-naoki-mori-make-that-23/ |access-date=5 September 2022 |website=Retraction Watch}}</ref><ref>{{cite journal | doi=10.1016/j.bbrc.2007.10.105 | volume=364 | issue=4 | title=RETRACTED: Downregulation of citrin, a mitochondrial AGC, is associated with apoptosis of hepatocytes | journal=Biochemical and Biophysical Research Communications | pages=937–944 | pmid=18273444 | last1 = Sawada | first1 = S | last2 = Kinjo | first2 = T | last3 = Makishi | first3 = S | last4 = Tomita | first4 = M | last5 = Arasaki | first5 = A | last6 = Iseki | first6 = K | last7 = Watanabe | first7 = H | last8 = Kobayashi | first8 = K | last9 = Sunakawa | first9 = H | last10 = Iwamasa | first10 = T | last11 = Mori | first11 = N| year=2007 | doi-access = free | hdl = 20.500.12000/2807 | hdl-access = free }}{{Retracted|doi=10.1016/j.bbrc.2011.08.005|pmid=21843506|http://retractionwatch.com/2011/10/10/another-retraction-for-naoki-mori-make-that-23/ ''Retraction Watch''|http://retractionwatch.com/category/by-author/naoki-mori-retractions/ ''Retraction Watch''|intentional=yes}}</ref> Mori took "full responsibility" for "multiple inaccurate and inappropriately duplicated" images,<ref>{{cite web | first = Paul | last = Jump | url = http://www.timeshighereducation.co.uk/story.asp?sectioncode=26&storycode=414802&c=1 | title = 'Manipulation' nets virologist a 10-year journal ban | work = [[Times Higher Education]] | date = 13 January 2011 | access-date = 27 October 2011}}</ref> and was dismissed from his university post in August 2010.<ref name="science"/>

Mori contested his dismissal in court, and the University of the Ryukyus instead imposed a 10-month suspension.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Normile |first=Dennis |date=7 March 2011 |title=Dismissed Virologist Gets Job Back |url=https://www.science.org/content/article/dismissed-virologist-gets-job-back |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211105221652/https://www.science.org/content/article/dismissed-virologist-gets-job-back |archive-date=5 November 2021 |access-date=5 September 2022 |website=[[Science (journal)|Science]] |publisher=[[American Association for the Advancement of Science|AAAS]]}}</ref> Mori was rehired in March 2011 and had resumed publishing by April 2012<ref>{{Cite web |last=Marcus |first=Adam |date=6 April 2012 |title=Back in the saddle: After more than 30 retractions, Naoki Mori publishing again |url=http://retractionwatch.com/2012/04/06/back-in-the-saddle-after-30-retractions-naoki-mori-publishing-again/ |access-date=5 September 2022 |website=Retraction Watch}}</ref> with a research paper titled "Honokiol induces cell cycle arrest and apoptosis via inhibition of survival signals in adult T-cell leukemia".<ref>{{cite journal | doi=10.1016/j.bbagen.2012.03.009 | pmid=22465179 | volume=1820 | issue=7 | title=Honokiol induces cell cycle arrest and apoptosis via inhibition of survival signals in adult T-cell leukemia | journal=Biochimica et Biophysica Acta (BBA) - General Subjects | pages=879–887| year=2012 | last1=Ishikawa | first1=Chie | last2=Arbiser | first2=Jack L. | last3=Mori | first3=Naoki }}</ref>

